From: xPDFSDK team <noreply@xpdfsdk.local>
Date: 2026-06-20
Subject: [PATCH ship-0016] Handle stacked rectangle no-op clips

Background
==========
R9 added no-op clip elision for a single rectangle clip, but device logs for
`error.pdf` p2/p3 showed `noopClips=0` while `/Meta20` still had
`clips=28071` and `clipSwitches=28071`. Inspecting the decoded QDF stream
showed a Form-wide rectangular clip near the start of `/Meta20`, but PDFium's
parsed `CPDF_ClipPath` can hold stacked inherited clip components rather than
one path.

This patch
==========
1. Keeps the same feature flag, fallback behavior, and `noopClips` telemetry.
2. Extends `ClipPathIsNoOpForObjectBounds()` from one rectangle path to a stack
   of rectangle-like clip paths.
3. Computes the intersection of those clip rectangles and elides the clip only
   if the intersection still contains the path object's bounds.
4. Still fails closed for text clips, empty clips, or any non-rectangle clip
   component.

For the Meta20 stream sampled from `error.pdf`, this is the narrower fix for
R9's miss: inherited rectangle clipping should become a no-op for each tiny
path node, collapsing `clips` / `clipSwitches` and lowering `replayMs`.

---
 .../render/veloce_path_display_list.cpp       | 28 +++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 22 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/core/fpdfapi/render/veloce_path_display_list.cpp b/core/fpdfapi/render/veloce_path_display_list.cpp
index 418fdb9b0..c47ec912a 100644
--- a/core/fpdfapi/render/veloce_path_display_list.cpp
+++ b/core/fpdfapi/render/veloce_path_display_list.cpp
@@ -344,20 +344,36 @@ bool ClipPathIsNoOpForObjectBounds(const CPDF_ClipPath& clip_path,
   if (!clip_path.HasRef()) {
     return true;
   }
-  if (clip_path.GetTextCount() != 0 || clip_path.GetPathCount() != 1) {
+  if (clip_path.GetTextCount() != 0 || clip_path.GetPathCount() == 0) {
     return false;
   }
 
-  CPDF_Path clip_path_data = clip_path.GetPath(0);
-  if (!clip_path_data.GetObject() || !clip_path_data.IsRect()) {
+  std::optional<CFX_FloatRect> clip_bounds;
+  for (size_t i = 0; i < clip_path.GetPathCount(); ++i) {
+    CPDF_Path clip_path_data = clip_path.GetPath(i);
+    const CFX_Path* path = clip_path_data.GetObject();
+    if (!path) {
+      return false;
+    }
+    std::optional<CFX_FloatRect> rect = path->GetRect(nullptr);
+    if (!rect.has_value()) {
+      return false;
+    }
+    if (clip_bounds.has_value()) {
+      clip_bounds->Intersect(rect.value());
+    } else {
+      clip_bounds = rect.value();
+    }
+  }
+
+  if (!clip_bounds.has_value()) {
     return false;
   }
 
-  CFX_FloatRect clip_bounds = clip_path_data.GetBoundingBox();
   CFX_FloatRect normalized_object_bounds = object_bounds;
-  clip_bounds.Normalize();
+  clip_bounds->Normalize();
   normalized_object_bounds.Normalize();
-  return clip_bounds.Contains(normalized_object_bounds);
+  return clip_bounds->Contains(normalized_object_bounds);
 }
 
 bool RequiresTransparency(const CPDF_PageObject* obj) {
